 "text": "Hi, how have you been? It' not ideal, but as long as you follow the rules, you' usually fine. Pick a flat spot in the grass, and ask permission from the funeral home before you go. Bring your own food and a few drinks, and keep the noise down. Some cemeteries even charge a fee for picking a spot. Keep it to an earshot of yourselves, and don't use a loud speaker. The big fear is getting caught and being asked to leave. If that happens, pick up and move on.",
